# Instructions for AI assistants
You are assisting with creating structured university lecture notes and cheat sheets in this repository.

Always follow the guidelines and templates located in `.templates/`:
- `.templates/GUIDELINES.md` — Style guide and structural requirements.
- `.templates/LECTURE_TEMPLATE.md` — Detailed lecture note template (`README.md`).
- `.templates/CHEATSHEET_TEMPLATE.md` — Concise summary & cheat sheet template (`cheat-sheet.md`).

Key rules:
1. Every lecture/module must contain both `README.md` (detailed note) and `cheat-sheet.md` (summary & cheat sheet).
2. The `cheat-sheet.md` MUST capture the most important essence of the topic (TL;DR, core concepts, definitions, architectural principles, comparative tables, rules of thumb, gotchas/pitfalls), EVEN IF there are no formulas in that topic. If formulas exist, include a comprehensive formula table.
3. Maintain the progression: Intuition ("plain english / analogies") -> Rigorous Math (KaTeX `$ ... $`) -> Circuit Implementation / Diagrams -> Pitfalls & Real-world usage.
4. Keep navigation bars at the top and bottom of each document.

